      "paragraphs": 3,
      "prompt": "Write an English project handoff of 200 to 260 words in exactly three prose paragraphs, without headings or lists. Preserve every fact in this brief. You may explain the distinctions between pending work and completion, or between the two owners, but add no new facts, commitments, causes, schedules or procedures. Brief: Imani owns the database migration. Theo owns the documentation update. The migration is blocked until backup verification finishes. Verification is pending. Documentation work may continue meanwhile. The migration has not been confirmed complete, and deployment has not been confirmed. The staging environment is available for documentation screenshots; this does not establish production readiness. The current public guide is version 1.7. Theo's planned update is version 1.8, which has not been published. Do not swap owners, claim all work must stop, promise a deployment time, invent a checklist or claim the pending backup has passed verification.",
